  "long-sentence | banks/elements.ts | You carry a light pack: a weaker day-master that thrives in good company, the cyclist riding in the group rather than alone into the wind. Choosing your allies is choosing your strength.",
  "long-sentence | banks/topics/depth.ts | Every day carries one of twelve animal signs, and your birth chart holds four, one for each part of life. When today's sign sits directly opposite one of yours, the two pull against each other. The Complete Guide to the Three Fates calls these signs that strike each other and counts them as mostly trouble, which is why this page spends its words on what to do about it.",
  "long-sentence | banks/topics/depth.ts | The old calendars follow the element at the centre of your birth chart through twelve stages, like a life from first steps to rest, and each day lands you on one of them. The Complete Guide to the Three Fates, a sixteenth-century handbook, describes this stage as the point where things start to flourish, like a young person dressing as an adult for the first time.",
  "long-sentence | banks/topics/depth.ts | To be straight with you: this one usually lands harder on you than on most people, because your birth chart already carries this same tug between those two parts of life.",
  "long-sentence | glossary.ts |  are the old calendars' names for the ten ways a passing stem can meet yours — the same cast of ten relations, rotating with the days, months, and years.",
  "long-sentence | glossary.ts | Each day and season carries an element too. When it feeds or matches yours, the line says it suits you; when it drains or crowds yours, the day runs against your grain and asks a gentler pace.",
  "long-sentence | glossary.ts | Every other note is measured against it: elements feed or drain it, passing stems meet it as one of the ten gods, and strong or weak describes its backing. When a reading says 'you', this is the you it means.",
  "long-sentence | glossary.ts | The old calendars split the day into twelve two-hour blocks, and each block carries one of the twelve animal signs — the rat from 11 pm, the ox from 1 am, and so on around the clock.",
  "long-sentence | glossary.ts | The seven rings are the days ahead: a solid green ring leans your way, a dashed amber ring is a day to take slower, and a faint ring sits even. The filled one is the day on screen; tap any ring to open that day.",
  "long-sentence | glossary.ts | The ten gods (十神) are the old calendars' names for the ten ways a passing stem can meet yours — the same cast of ten relations, rotating with the days, months, and years.",
  "long-sentence | glossary.ts | The twelve Day Officers are the old almanac's rotation: each day takes the next of twelve roles in a fixed cycle, from setting stakes to drawing the shutters.",
  "long-sentence | glossary.ts | The twelve life stages track where a stem stands in its cycle — first growth through peak to rest and back — the way a day moves through morning, noon, and night.",
  "long-sentence | glossary.ts | Two of those blocks stand out on any day. The one whose sign clashes with the day's own sign is the rough hour, where plans tend to jostle; the one whose sign combines with it is the easy hour, a quieter window for anything that needs agreeing.",
  "long-sentence | marks.ts | The seven rings are the days ahead: a solid green ring leans your way, a dashed amber ring is a day to take slower, and a faint ring sits even. The filled one is the day on screen; tap any ring to open that day.",
  "long-sentence | read-more.ts | A clash day tends to arrive as scheduling friction made visible: the meeting that moves, the plan that collides with a better one, the thing you postponed refusing to stay postponed.",
  "long-sentence | read-more.ts | A punishment rarely announces itself as an event — it shows up as a mood with a return ticket: the same small irritation, the same conversation you keep almost having.",
  "long-sentence | read-more.ts | A trine reads as alignment you didn't have to arrange: the group agrees faster than usual, the pieces you've been holding separately admit they belong together.",
  "long-sentence | rendered: chart page | A self-punishment sits on dragon–dragon in your home palace and home palace — the bar you keep raising on yourself after everyone else has gone home. When this room aches, look first at your own grip.",
  "long-sentence | rendered: chart page | Three checks sit behind that reading: you were born in a season that doesn't feed your element out of season; you have ground under you — your own element hides inside your branches rooted; and you field a small team — few of the visible stems are on your side outnumbered. Only 1 of the three runs in your favor, so the chart reads weak — light, not lacking.",
  "long-sentence | rendered: chart page | Three checks sit behind that reading: you were born in a season that doesn't feed your element out of season; you have ground under you — your own element hides inside your branches rooted; and you field a small team — few of the visible stems are on your side outnumbered. Only 1 of the three runs in your favor, so the chart reads weak, though by a narrow margin — a close call, not a clear one — light, not lacking.",
  "long-sentence | rendered: chart page | Three checks sit behind that reading: you were born in a season that doesn't feed your element out of season; you have ground under you — your own element hides inside your branches rooted; and you have allies — most of the visible stems are on your side backed. Only 2 of the three run in your favor, so the chart reads weak — light, not lacking.",
